## Golden: copiar un `string` owned emite el `share` del binding copiado.
##
## `pengu_cow_string_share` es un no-op para SDS, pero la copia de un `string`
## local emite `pengu_string_share_value`, que le da al binding copiado su
## propio buffer: el `banish` de los dos es seguro.
import std.spark

rune Holder:
    name as string

weave main into int:
    var a as string is "hola" + " mundo"
    var b as string is a
    calling spark.println with b
    banish a
    banish b
    var h as Holder is with name is ("cam" + "po")
    calling spark.println with h.name
    banish h.name
    return 0
